.nh
.TH hclapi 8

.SH NAME
hclapi \- Declarative API runtime that turns HCL manifests into structured HTTP services.


.SH SYNOPSIS
hclapi

.PP
\fBUsage\fP:

.EX
hclapi [GLOBAL OPTIONS] [command [COMMAND OPTIONS]] [ARGUMENTS...]
.EE


.SH COMMANDS
.SH serve
Start the hclapi HTTP server.

.PP
\fB--config, -c, --manifests, -m\fP="": Path to .hcl file, or directory containing manifests. (default: ".")

.PP
\fB--host, -h\fP="": Host address to bind the server (overrides manifest).

.PP
\fB--port, -p\fP="": Port to bind the server (overrides manifest). (default: 0)

.PP
\fB--verbose, -v\fP: Enable verbose debug logging.

.SH openapi
Export the compiled OpenAPI 3.1 specification for your manifests.

.PP
\fB--config, -c, --manifests, -m\fP="": Path to .hcl file or directory containing manifests. (default: ".")

.PP
\fB--format, -f\fP="": Output format: json or yaml. (default: "json")

.PP
\fB--output, -o\fP="": Path to output file (defaults to stdout).

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP: Pretty-print JSON output.

.SH version, v
Show detailed version information.
